{"title":"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of a circle center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is any point on the circle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6cd34a211696ff9f8dbf820fb384c0acd73967b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOC \\not\\le 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the chord which is the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. The line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c5f98c6f70b855ea3d874c757247f6dfbbac5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, then it is also the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the reflection of D across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca59404fdefc2f3d435a609b6a8f713931e32414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OAJ = \\angle OAC = \\angle ACO = \\angle AOD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"294\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e8783e3abcf90208ba5930dfaf086b24d1fdc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAJO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119dee34ef12ed77df6ab14d95358266f5cd7dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DFJE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> is also a parallelogram with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0cf271838cdaf87036195ab99e55a9ef9499bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEF = \\angle EFJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />, then it suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f244be398f47f56f174eb413a1a20e72fefd47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEF = \\frac1{2} \\angle EFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee71917fb550aa758b8324199364a2928c1d2e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA = AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979c6deb11752ef4146e52440d2955ee0beead13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Further observe that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d950cd766423161832d5ec77ff122040fcd8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e71b4c748a5b1ca67a756e5ca20f6bf0f062b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFO$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> are equilateral. Finally, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a200a35220ba75fa69159c8d364db081c387fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEF = \\frac1{2} \\angle DOF = \\frac1{2} (\\angle DOA + 60^{\\circ}) = \\frac1{2} (\\angle OAC + \\angle EAO) = \\frac1{2} \\angle EAC = \\frac1{2} \\angle EFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"679\" height=\"38\" />, \n</p><p>as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO\" title=\"2002 IMO\">2002 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201018\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 190/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5537/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\